#### Reported Bug #1

| Issue ID | Date Reported | Module | Issue Description | Severity | Assigned To | Status | Resolution Date | Reference-1 (Image) | Reference-2 (Video) | Notes | Additional Notes |
|----------|---------------|---------|-------------------|----------|-------------|--------|-----------------|--------------------|--------------------|-------|------------------|
| BUG-004 | 19-Jul-2026 | After Sales → Receive Payment → MFS Payment | The system allows users to enter and submit any payment amount when selecting MFS Payment methods (bKash, Nagad, Rocket). No validation exists to check the maximum transaction limit supported by the selected MFS provider. For example, a user can record a bKash payment amount exceeding the provider's allowed transaction limit. The system should validate the payment amount against configurable MFS limits and prevent submission when the entered amount exceeds the allowed limit. | Medium | Developer Team | Open | | | | Missing business-rule validation for MFS payment limits. | Recommended to maintain configurable transaction limits per MFS provider and validate payment amounts during payment entry. |

